      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "Polyphia clears RADAR because the instrument is the language. Tim Henson and Scott LePage treat electric guitar as melody, percussion and production surface at once, folding prog precision into trap-derived rhythm, electronic texture and heavy-guitar vocabulary without reducing the music to technique for technique's sake. BE NOT AFRAID gives the Washington date a genuinely current center: the band has described this record as a more communal writing process, with everyone in the room earlier instead of assembling separate ideas after the fact. Echostage also makes sense for a group whose music depends as much on bass pressure and pocket as on fretboard detail.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for the rescheduled local date if March is open. This is a strong DMV night for guitar, rhythm and modern heavy music, but the same North American run passes through Philadelphia and Brooklyn just days earlier, so there is no need to treat Washington as a scarce regional opportunity.",
